        "looking-glass-book",
        "chameleon-person"
      ],
      "note": "British literature is a central source of inspiration for this band, drawing on their English background and the characters and stories you both grew up with. Alice in Wonderland is a whole category, with more works and media references to come.\n\nYou connect their current interest in being twelve with girlhood in stories that are surreal and strange: knowing yourself while being told who to be, not being taken seriously, and navigating contradictory expectations of women.\n\nYou want to develop these childhood references into a world that explores those tensions.\n\nConnections should show a clear shared category, like the overlap of a Venn diagram. A giant floral hat would belong to both floral and hats; a loose thematic association is not enough.",
      "noteAuthor": "saved-user-summary",
      "noteSource": "design-previews/say-now/portfolio-original/index.html#flowers-details",
      "thumbnail": "thumbnails/castle-heirlooms.jpg"
    },
